  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "$x$ is a prime **and** less than $15$, **and** $x$ is odd.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is prime\n\n- $L(x):$ $x$ is less than $15$\n\n- $O(x):$ $x$ is odd",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:**  $x$ is a prime and less than $15.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\,\\text{is prime}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\,\\text{is less than }15}_{⏟}}_{L},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧L.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is odd. This corresponds to $O.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is a prime and less than }15}_{⏟}}_{P∧L}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\,\\text{is odd }}_{⏟}}_{O},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧L∧O.$",
